    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 🚀 Ultimate n8n Agentic RAG Template (v2 — Improved)\n\n**Improvements applied:**\n\n1. **Polling triggers** — bumped from every minute to every 5 minutes to reduce Drive API quota burn.\n2. **Switch routing gap fixed** — `text/csv` is now an explicit case (output 3); Google Docs/fallback bumped to output 4. CSV files no longer mis-route to the text extractor.\n3. **Tabular data now embedded** — After schema update completes, tabular content flows into the Supabase vectorstore so RAG can find spreadsheet context semantically.\n4. **Race condition fixed** — Tabular branch is now fully sequential: Summarize → Set Schema → Update Schema → Insert into Vectorstore. No parallel fanout.\n5. **Error handling added** — `Download File`, `Insert into Supabase Vectorstore`, and `Insert Table Rows` all have `onError: continueErrorOutput`. Three Set Error nodes capture failure context. Wire them to Slack/email as needed.\n6. **Delete filter fixed** — `Delete Old Doc Rows` now uses `eq` instead of `like` for exact file_id matching. Stale chunks will now reliably be removed.\n7. **Chunk size explicit** — Character Text Splitter is set to 800 chars / 160 overlap (~20%). Tune these for your content density.\n8. **Session ID hardened** — Falls back to `$execution.id + timestamp` if no sessionId is provided, preventing all anonymous users from sharing a single memory key.\n9. **System prompt hardened** — Explicit tool selection order (RAG first → List Docs → Get File → SQL), citation rules ([Source: title]), and a structured \"not found\" fallback response.\n\n## Getting Started\n1. Run the table creation nodes first\n2. Upload documents to the watched Google Drive folder\n3. Wire the error Set nodes to a notification channel\n4. Start chatting",
        "height": 1320,
        "width": 540,
        "color": 6
      },
